## Why This Is Asked

This question adds counting of optimal partitions to a standard min-max DP, testing both correctness and edge-case handling in a realistic workload-balancing scenario.

## Key Concepts

- DP with a value-cost pair (minCost, count) and prefix sums for O(1) subarray sums
- Top-down memoization and bottom-up tabulation with identical transitions
- Edge-case handling: n<k invalid, zeros, large sums

## Code Example

```javascript
function minCostPartitions(nums, k){
  const n = nums.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1]=pref[i]+nums[i];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array.from({length:k+1},()=>null));
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) dp[i][1] = {best: pref[i], count:1};
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let j=2;j<=Math.min(i,k);j++){
      let best = Infinity, cnt = 0;
      for(let t=j-1;t<=i-1;t++){
        const last = pref[i]-pref[t];
        const prev = dp[t][j-1];
        if(!prev) continue;
        const cand = Math.max(prev.best, last);
        if(cand < best){ best = cand; cnt = prev.count; }
        else if(cand === best){ cnt += prev.count; }
      }
      dp[i][j] = {best, count: cnt};
    }
  }
  const res = dp[n][k];
  return res ? {cost: res.best, ways: res.count} : null;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you modify to return all partition indices achieving the min cost?
- Could you optimize to O(nk) time with a narrowed search if nums are non-decreasing?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical graph DP with a real-world flavor (service startup), ensuring knowledge of cycle detection, topological order, and dynamic programming.

## Key Concepts

- Topological sort (Kahn/DFS)
- DAG DP for path/finish times
- Cycle detection via processed node count

## Code Example

```javascript
function earliestStartup(graph, startup, t) {
  const V = graph.length;
  const indeg = new Array(V).fill(0);
  for (let u = 0; u < V; u++) for (const v of graph[u]) indeg[v]++;
  const q = [];
  const earliest = startup.slice();
  for (let i = 0; i < V; i++) if (indeg[i] === 0) q.push(i);
  let seen = 0;
  while (q.length) {
    const u = q.shift();
    seen++;
    for (const v of graph[u]) {
      earliest[v] = Math.max(earliest[v], earliest[u] + startup[v]);
      if (--indeg[v] === 0) q.push(v);
    }
  }
  if (seen !== V) throw new Error('cycle detected');
  return earliest[t];
}
```

